01:04:50.130 --> 01:04:51.270
Since you're passing by,

01:04:51.830 --> 01:04:53.951
Then I'll ask you a personal question.

01:04:54.991 --> 01:04:56.772
Could you be the great grasshopper?

01:04:57.312 --> 01:04:57.552
Yes,

01:04:57.612 --> 01:04:58.713
SO ?

01:04:58.733 --> 01:05:00.493
It's curious how people change.

01:05:00.494 --> 01:05:02.314
because when I met you three years ago,

01:05:02.315 --> 01:05:03.675
You were less grumpy.

01:05:04.235 --> 01:05:07.576
You were making films called Les Pissanlits par la Racine,

01:05:07.676 --> 01:05:08.937
The Gun-Toting Uncles,

01:05:08.957 --> 01:05:09.757
The Spies.

01:05:09.758 --> 01:05:09.877
Yes.

01:05:10.377 --> 01:05:11.337
You become a star.

01:05:11.577 --> 01:05:11.817
The other one,

01:05:11.837 --> 01:05:12.278
Neremois,

01:05:12.298 --> 01:05:14.758
This is of great interest to us regarding a question of gas route.

01:05:15.519 --> 01:05:17.419
But this can even be seen in the newspapers.

01:05:17.499 --> 01:05:18.199
because now,

01:05:18.200 --> 01:05:21.060
There are, however, entire pages dedicated to Mireille Dard.

01:05:21.120 --> 01:05:22.581
I only want one example.

01:05:23.301 --> 01:05:23.641
Besides,

01:05:23.642 --> 01:05:24.721
I apologize for having to tell you this,

01:05:24.761 --> 01:05:25.161
dear friend,

01:05:25.261 --> 01:05:26.202
but in your articles,

01:05:26.203 --> 01:05:27.862
You're acting silly when it's not allowed.

01:05:27.922 --> 01:05:30.343
because we do read some curious things.

01:05:31.223 --> 01:05:32.844
I used to be so ugly,

01:05:33.004 --> 01:05:33.384
skinny,

01:05:33.484 --> 01:05:34.804
gaunt and bony,

01:05:34.824 --> 01:05:36.965
that I didn't dare undress on the beaches.

01:05:36.966 --> 01:05:37.545
It's true.

01:05:37.961 --> 01:05:39.042
Because of this complex,

01:05:39.043 --> 01:05:40.263
I hadn't learned to swim.

01:05:40.543 --> 01:05:42.165
I've only known how to swim since this summer.

01:05:42.325 --> 01:05:42.825
So, we

01:05:42.865 --> 01:05:43.265
I don't know,

01:05:43.305 --> 01:05:43.966
but in sales,

01:05:43.967 --> 01:05:45.988
It seems like you've known how to swim for a bit longer than that.

01:05:45.989 --> 01:05:52.573
In 1968,

01:05:53.274 --> 01:05:56.076
in the same magazine where Mireille d'Arc chose to pose nude,

01:05:56.857 --> 01:06:01.040
The dialogue writer addresses a love letter to the actress in his own way.

01:06:03.362 --> 01:06:04.423
"Hey there, my pretty one"

01:06:04.543 --> 01:06:05.584
by Michel Audiard.

01:06:07.165 --> 01:06:07.985
I'm discovering it with you.

01:06:09.946 --> 01:06:10.246
Hey,

01:06:10.266 --> 01:06:10.746
my pretty one,

01:06:11.486 --> 01:06:14.627
when I see you perched like a radiator cap on the hood of a Rolls,

01:06:16.528 --> 01:06:17.648
You can imagine how much I'm laughing.

01:06:18.648 --> 01:06:23.650
When I read in the press that you are now an international star simply because you are working with Americans,

01:06:23.970 --> 01:06:25.310
You can imagine how much I'm laughing.

01:06:26.291 --> 01:06:26.871
Your car,

01:06:26.872 --> 01:06:27.591
in life, by the way,

01:06:27.631 --> 01:06:29.151
You didn't mention my car.

01:06:29.171 --> 01:06:30.932
You say "my car" or "my car".

01:06:31.132 --> 01:06:32.092
Never my car.

01:06:33.173 --> 01:06:33.753
In my day,

01:06:33.754 --> 01:06:34.673
She was saying the car.

01:06:35.969 --> 01:06:36.409
Your tire,

01:06:36.449 --> 01:06:39.090
It's the little white Minimoque in which I gladly see you again.

01:06:39.091 --> 01:06:40.591
the one where I learned to drive,

01:06:41.511 --> 01:06:42.312
as it is in yourself.

01:06:44.173 --> 01:06:44.873
I was on my bicycle,

01:06:44.913 --> 01:06:45.473
Do you understand?

01:06:46.033 --> 01:06:46.654
The Minimoque,

01:06:46.674 --> 01:06:46.974
the bicycle,

01:06:47.034 --> 01:06:47.654
That's our thing.

01:06:48.334 --> 01:06:49.955
The same goes for the international star.

01:06:50.735 --> 01:06:51.756
You will never be,

01:06:51.816 --> 01:06:52.396
You're worth more.

01:06:53.236 --> 01:06:53.516
Come on,

01:06:53.517 --> 01:06:53.677
of art!

01:06:55.397 --> 01:06:55.637
Come on,

01:06:55.717 --> 01:06:56.538
Go on !

01:06:56.738 --> 01:06:56.938
Come on,

01:06:56.998 --> 01:06:57.518
my darling,

01:06:57.678 --> 01:06:57.958
Go on !

01:06:58.679 --> 01:06:59.939
Just like in real life!

01:07:02.840 --> 01:07:03.381
A star,

01:07:03.701 --> 01:07:04.261
Like you said.

01:07:05.028 --> 01:07:05.548
What is this ?

01:07:06.109 --> 01:07:06.989
This is Mother Taylor,

01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:07.910
She is fat.

01:07:07.970 --> 01:07:08.670
She speaks falsely.

01:07:08.971 --> 01:07:10.031
No one notices.

01:07:10.432 --> 01:07:11.993
If you say a single wrong word,

01:07:12.293 --> 01:07:13.174
They'll come down on you.

01:07:13.374 --> 01:07:13.994
And we're right.

01:07:14.634 --> 01:07:15.535
You have to play it right.

01:07:15.575 --> 01:07:16.556
You must speak truthfully.

01:07:16.636 --> 01:07:17.636
You must be thin.

01:07:17.817 --> 01:07:18.817
You must be exciting.

01:07:18.897 --> 01:07:22.059
Because you are Mireille Dark and you will never be a Taylor.

01:07:25.142 --> 01:07:26.763
When he played that game with Mireille,

01:07:26.803 --> 01:07:28.464
It was never true.

01:07:28.844 --> 01:07:30.045
It was a joke.

01:07:30.465 --> 01:07:31.866
He was saying to her, "Come on, you slut!"

01:07:32.366 --> 01:07:33.347
How do you say that to someone?

01:07:33.387 --> 01:07:34.548
But that's what he called it.

01:07:34.908 --> 01:07:38.330
And it was obviously without any malice or ulterior motive.

01:07:38.611 --> 01:07:39.871
He adored Mireille.

01:07:40.492 --> 01:07:40.932
Mireille d'Arc,

01:07:40.952 --> 01:07:43.654
when Michel Audiab tells you some hard truths in a newspaper,

01:07:43.714 --> 01:07:44.615
How are you feeling?

01:07:45.035 --> 01:07:45.435
Alright,

01:07:46.216 --> 01:07:46.616
I like it.

01:07:47.657 --> 01:07:49.318
Because he says them with great tenderness,

01:07:49.458 --> 01:07:50.439
Very kind.

01:07:52.060 --> 01:07:54.922
But it's a little bit hard to accept, especially since it's still difficult to accept.

01:07:54.942 --> 01:07:55.442
No way,

01:07:55.482 --> 01:07:56.903
He said you are not Lys Taylor,

01:07:56.904 --> 01:07:58.124
You will never be Lys Taylor,

01:07:58.144 --> 01:07:59.024
But you are Mireille d'Arc,

01:07:59.085 --> 01:08:00.145
That's actually a compliment.

01:08:01.766 --> 01:08:04.148
That means I'm not copying Lys Taylor or anyone else.

01:08:05.312 --> 01:08:07.794
He recognizes what she is becoming,

01:08:07.814 --> 01:08:08.554
That's what's great about it.

01:08:09.155 --> 01:08:11.736
He notes that she is no longer the little girl he once knew.

01:08:12.077 --> 01:08:13.818
but that she has become someone else,

01:08:13.918 --> 01:08:14.418
a large one.

01:08:14.819 --> 01:08:15.139
It's good,

01:08:15.199 --> 01:08:15.899
Mr. Audiard,

01:08:15.900 --> 01:08:17.140
You can see that it works for me.

01:08:18.341 --> 01:08:21.443
I see that I am becoming a star because they are starting to treat me.

01:08:22.584 --> 01:08:23.685
You're going to make us laugh at the dinner table.

01:08:24.345 --> 01:08:24.625
Hold,

01:08:24.685 --> 01:08:25.726
Come sit here.

01:08:25.727 --> 01:08:26.947
Cinema,

01:08:27.027 --> 01:08:29.488
It's not such a bad life.

01:08:29.549 --> 01:08:31.470
Mireille Dark always has a great time with her group.

01:08:32.150 --> 01:08:34.452
But she could easily see herself riding a new wave.

01:08:35.144 --> 01:08:35.944
towards a different kind of cinema.

01:08:36.605 --> 01:08:38.445
I'm starting to get a little bored with them.

01:08:38.846 --> 01:08:39.326
At the same time,

01:08:39.327 --> 01:08:40.406
I love them deeply.

01:08:40.606 --> 01:08:41.066
That's not it.

01:08:41.507 --> 01:08:47.169
But I want to have a more different role.

01:08:49.150 --> 01:08:55.072
So I have a producer who has contracts with me and I tell him I would like to make a film with Godard.

01:08:57.753 --> 01:08:58.473
Brigitte Bardot,

01:08:58.594 --> 01:09:00.174
to whom this image has been imposed,

01:09:00.214 --> 01:09:02.055
finally, who was trapped in this image,

01:09:02.495 --> 01:09:04.356
What is she suddenly doing overnight?

01:09:04.940 --> 01:09:06.721
She breaks all that and says,

01:09:07.601 --> 01:09:08.061
finished,

01:09:08.241 --> 01:09:08.641
It's over.

01:09:08.741 --> 01:09:10.181
like a kind of counterpoint.

01:09:11.022 --> 01:09:11.402
Mireille,

01:09:11.422 --> 01:09:12.922
It's much thinner than that.

01:09:13.142 --> 01:09:14.303
She has the intelligence to tell herself,

01:09:14.343 --> 01:09:14.783
Well, for me,

01:09:15.323 --> 01:09:16.543
They won't lock me up in there.

01:09:16.544 --> 01:09:21.465
He's someone who never stayed within the boxes that were offered to him.

01:09:21.466 --> 01:09:22.365
who took risks,

01:09:22.425 --> 01:09:24.726
even if it means breaking an image that was already in place,

01:09:24.786 --> 01:09:26.786
a woman who knew how to reinvent herself.

01:09:27.466 --> 01:09:28.607
In trying to reinvent itself,

01:09:29.247 --> 01:09:32.948
The actress is aware that she is denying her past and distancing herself from her uncles.

01:09:33.804 --> 01:09:36.446
Especially since the new wave keeps destroying their films.

01:09:37.026 --> 01:09:38.287
This is what you call "old-fashioned" cinema.

01:09:38.568 --> 01:09:43.912
We must not forget that Rodiard was vilified by the entire press for years.

01:09:44.712 --> 01:09:46.434
He was called a vulgar writer,

01:09:46.454 --> 01:09:47.875
of a vulgar dialogue writer.

01:09:47.975 --> 01:09:48.715
I had done

01:09:49.436 --> 01:09:50.637
20-22 films,

01:09:50.697 --> 01:09:52.198
I was just getting by like that.

01:09:52.298 --> 01:09:53.619
Nobody was talking about it much,

01:09:53.620 --> 01:09:55.100
It wasn't so bad, actually.

01:09:55.600 --> 01:09:57.322
And then one day, disaster struck.

01:09:57.342 --> 01:09:59.924
There are two or three idiots who have me in their sights.

01:10:01.324 --> 01:10:03.285
And let's keep that from the new wave if we want.

01:10:03.666 --> 01:10:05.967
They prepared me for all the films I was making,

01:10:05.968 --> 01:10:06.808
of those that I didn't do.

01:10:07.228 --> 01:10:08.449
They haven't stopped talking about me.

01:10:08.509 --> 01:10:12.992
Finally, the theme, if you will, was that the baseness of Monsieur Odière attracts the large audience.

01:10:13.313 --> 01:10:15.234
In what ways do you identify with the new wave?

01:10:15.414 --> 01:10:16.175
Well, I owe him a lot.

01:10:16.715 --> 01:10:23.120
We all knew young people at that time who wanted to remake cinema and who thought a lot.

01:10:25.001 --> 01:10:29.104
They thought a great deal, and that was their main occupation.

01:10:29.496 --> 01:10:31.037
We really get the impression that currently,

01:10:31.217 --> 01:10:32.538
In France,

01:10:33.298 --> 01:10:33.638
at least,

01:10:34.239 --> 01:10:35.720
two main filming methods.

01:10:35.800 --> 01:10:37.621
His own and that of a Lelouch,

01:10:37.661 --> 01:10:38.361
For example,

01:10:38.901 --> 01:10:40.022
not to mention Godard.

01:10:40.302 --> 01:10:40.922
Why Lelouch?

01:10:40.982 --> 01:10:41.703
Isn't that commercial?

01:10:43.024 --> 01:10:43.144
Ah,

01:10:43.145 --> 01:10:45.705
That's a question I can ask you as well.

01:10:46.466 --> 01:10:48.267
I don't know what you mean by commercial.

01:10:49.587 --> 01:10:51.849
First, it will be necessary to define it once and for all.

01:10:52.409 --> 01:10:53.489
What is the purpose of cinema?

01:10:54.930 --> 01:10:56.391
To be sold,

01:10:56.451 --> 01:10:56.571
Yes.

01:10:56.572 --> 01:10:56.691
Ah,

01:10:57.131 --> 01:10:57.812
So it's commercial.

01:10:59.596 --> 01:11:01.517
Those who claim not to be in business,

01:11:01.677 --> 01:11:03.498
What exactly do they want to do?

01:11:03.499 --> 01:11:04.198
Let them tell me.

01:11:04.199 --> 01:11:05.339
Art.

01:11:05.419 --> 01:11:05.579
Ah,

01:11:05.699 --> 01:11:06.980
of art.

01:11:07.120 --> 01:11:07.420
Me,

01:11:07.800 --> 01:11:08.500
I apologize,

01:11:08.540 --> 01:11:10.281
But I'm not there yet.

01:11:12.902 --> 01:11:15.363
Mireille wants to be directed by Jean-Luc Godard.

01:11:15.844 --> 01:11:17.584
the director of breathtaking masterpieces,

01:11:17.905 --> 01:11:18.605
and Pierrot Lefou.

01:11:20.186 --> 01:11:24.507
The meeting between the icon and the iconoclast is organized by the producer

01:11:25.008 --> 01:11:25.568
Raymond Danon.

01:11:26.060 --> 01:11:29.121
I think she needed to tell him she wanted something different.

01:11:29.141 --> 01:11:31.902
But all actresses go through a little bit of that.

01:11:32.022 --> 01:11:33.423
when you're in comedy,

01:11:33.483 --> 01:11:34.603
We want to go to Godard's,

01:11:34.663 --> 01:11:36.964
It was a dream come true for all actresses.

01:11:37.104 --> 01:11:37.604
Godard,

01:11:37.624 --> 01:11:39.385
I, for one, would have loved to work with Godard.

01:11:39.725 --> 01:11:40.965
The thing is, you have to,

01:11:42.526 --> 01:11:43.806
Cinema is a love story.

01:11:43.927 --> 01:11:47.068
A director needs to fall in love with us.

01:11:47.168 --> 01:11:47.888
In a way.

01:11:55.396 --> 01:11:56.098
Godard told me,

01:11:56.218 --> 01:11:56.619
Listen,

01:11:56.719 --> 01:11:57.922
You are everything I dislike.

01:11:58.583 --> 01:12:00.727
So if you want,

01:12:00.728 --> 01:12:01.950
We can make a film together.

01:12:04.804 --> 01:12:05.985
So I don't make him dream.

01:12:06.765 --> 01:12:08.205
I'm not his type of woman.

01:12:09.406 --> 01:12:13.088
So he's not going to make me seem more interesting than he finds me.

01:12:16.349 --> 01:12:19.370
Jean-Luc Godard has nothing but contempt for Mireille d'Arc.

01:12:21.531 --> 01:12:24.332
But he's looking for an unlikeable character for his next film.

01:12:25.553 --> 01:12:28.814
He offered her the role of a frivolous Parisian woman in Weekend,

01:12:29.495 --> 01:12:32.516
a satire that mocks the bourgeoisie and intellectuals.

01:12:35.489 --> 01:12:35.949
Silence,

01:12:35.950 --> 01:12:36.630
Please !

01:12:39.432 --> 01:12:39.952
Engine !

01:12:41.313 --> 01:12:47.738
Announcement !

01:12:47.758 --> 01:12:47.898
Galia,

01:12:47.938 --> 01:12:48.278
Where is she?

01:12:48.279 --> 01:12:49.619
Who attacked first?

01:12:49.699 --> 01:12:50.660
Israel or Egypt?

01:12:51.020 --> 01:12:52.101
These are the Egyptian accounts.

01:12:52.102 --> 01:12:52.821
Isn't that right, Roland?

01:12:53.022 --> 01:12:53.822
Poor ignorant man!

01:12:58.686 --> 01:12:59.526
One year after Galia,

01:13:00.347 --> 01:13:01.428
Mireille Dark and Corinne.

01:13:01.976 --> 01:13:02.857
Jean-Yann's wife,

01:13:03.417 --> 01:13:05.018
in this nightmarish road movie,

01:13:05.479 --> 01:13:09.021
where she weaves between bizarre encounters and car accidents.

01:13:10.843 --> 01:13:10.963
There,

01:13:10.983 --> 01:13:13.725
We were leaving Georges Lautner's group of friends,

01:13:13.985 --> 01:13:14.825
But it was Godard.

01:13:14.826 --> 01:13:15.166
She told me,

01:13:15.167 --> 01:13:16.627
I think it's going to be very complicated.

01:13:17.247 --> 01:13:18.288
because it's not easy.

01:13:20.029 --> 01:13:20.149
Me,

01:13:20.150 --> 01:13:21.450
I didn't hold it against Godard at all.

01:13:21.831 --> 01:13:22.571
who doesn't love me.

01:13:23.392 --> 01:13:23.872
I was thinking,

01:13:24.252 --> 01:13:25.613
It's me who wants to film with him.

01:13:25.633 --> 01:13:26.114
It's not him.

01:13:26.194 --> 01:13:26.394
SO,

01:13:26.974 --> 01:13:27.134
OK,

01:13:27.315 --> 01:13:27.735
All right,

01:13:27.736 --> 01:13:29.056
But he's still making the film with me.

01:13:31.296 --> 01:13:32.356
I was quite pleased.

01:13:34.937 --> 01:13:35.437
Engine !

01:13:36.818 --> 01:13:38.358
Announcement !

01:13:38.359 --> 01:13:39.198
There were evenings,

01:13:39.598 --> 01:13:42.979
I was almost dancing, thinking to myself, "That's it, I've discovered a different kind of cinema."

01:13:43.239 --> 01:13:45.000
I'm discovering another way of filming.

01:13:45.540 --> 01:13:49.881
I was discovering long takes that I had never done in my life.

01:13:51.362 --> 01:13:53.562
I don't think Godard was anything for her.

01:13:54.763 --> 01:13:56.863
It wasn't possible that he would actually recognize her.

01:13:58.544 --> 01:13:59.164
Godard is...

01:14:00.196 --> 01:14:01.997
To look for everything that is wrong with the person,

01:14:02.757 --> 01:14:03.898
And Mireille is the opposite.

01:14:03.978 --> 01:14:07.139
It's about seeing what a being can become at its most beautiful.

01:14:07.779 --> 01:14:10.000
So, for me, they are in an inverted world.

01:14:15.462 --> 01:14:16.503
Godard, I was an object.

01:14:16.703 --> 01:14:20.764
It was quite fun at a certain point to actually be an object,

01:14:20.804 --> 01:14:23.345
and then to have no responsibility whatsoever.

01:14:23.405 --> 01:14:23.806
It was nothing.

01:14:25.006 --> 01:14:28.347
And not having the right to participate in the discussion.

01:14:28.467 --> 01:14:28.668
Nothing,

01:14:28.768 --> 01:14:29.548
That is to say, really.

01:14:30.488 --> 01:14:35.171
You're here and they're using you like this.

01:14:35.172 --> 01:14:38.293
One can be a little masochistic.

01:14:39.954 --> 01:14:41.936
When she filmed Godard's Weekend,

01:14:42.896 --> 01:14:44.918
she wasn't afraid to tell Lautner

01:14:45.899 --> 01:14:46.679
"It's wonderful,

01:14:46.879 --> 01:14:49.101
Godard throws me in the mud.

01:14:49.102 --> 01:14:50.001
my vector,

01:14:50.021 --> 01:14:50.562
my jury.

01:14:51.682 --> 01:14:52.363
And for an actor,

01:14:52.443 --> 01:14:54.344
It was wonderful to find ourselves like that.

01:14:54.464 --> 01:14:59.588
confronted in a violent manner by a director who knew what he wanted.

01:14:59.968 --> 01:15:01.610
apparently involved in the drama.

01:15:02.150 --> 01:15:04.452
How can one work with both Lautner and Godard?

01:15:04.453 --> 01:15:05.173
That's so strange.

01:15:06.093 --> 01:15:10.878
That is to say, I wanted to work with Godard because I had made five films with Lautner.

01:15:12.099 --> 01:15:13.740
What I'm saying isn't meant to be malicious.

01:15:13.800 --> 01:15:15.522
because with Lautner,

01:15:16.863 --> 01:15:23.329
I felt like I had given everything I had to give because he was asking a large part of myself for it.

01:15:23.409 --> 01:15:27.192
a large degree of spontaneity.

